) receptor complex. <source>Cell Death Differ.</source> <volume>5</volume>:<fpage>271</fpage>&#x02013;288.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10200473</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal">Yeh, W.C., J.L. Pompa, M.E. McCurrach, H.B. Shu, A.J. Elia, A. Shahinian, M. Ng, A. Wakeham, W. Khoo, K. Mitchell, et al. <year>1998</year>. FADD: essential for embryo development and signaling from some, but not all, inducers of apoptosis. <source>Science.</source> <volume>279</volume>:<fpage>1954</fpage>&#x02013;1958.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9506948</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal">Yeh, W.C., A. Itie, A.J. Elia, M. Ng, H.B. Shu, A. Wakeham, C. Mirtsos, N. Suzuki, M. Bonnard, D.V. Goeddel, and T.W. Mak. <year>2000</year>. Requirement for Casper (c-FLIP) in regulation of death receptor-induced apoptosis and embryonic development. <source>Immunity.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>633</fpage>&#x02013;642.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10894163</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal">Varfolomeev, E.E., M. Schuchmann, V. Luria, N. Chiannilkulchai, J.S. Beckmann, I.L. Mett, D. Rebrikov, V.M. Brodianski, O.C. Kemper, O. Kollet, et al. <year>1998</year>. Targeted disruption of the mouse Caspase 8 gene ablates cell death induction by the TNF receptors, Fas/Apo1, and DR3 and is lethal prenatally. <source>Immunity.</source> <volume>9</volume>:<fpage>267</fpage>&#x02013;276.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9729047</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kataoka, T., R.C. Budd, N. Holler, M. Thome, F. Martinon, M. Irmler, K. Burns, M. Hahne, N. Kennedy, M. Kovacsovics, and J. Tschopp. <year>2000</year>. The caspase-8 inhibitor FLIP promotes activation of NF-kappaB and Erk signaling pathways. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>10</volume>:<fpage>640</fpage>&#x02013;648.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10837247</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal">Hu, W.H., H. Johnson, and H.B. Shu. <year>2000</year>. Activation of NF-kappaB by FADD, Casper, and caspase-8. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>275</volume>:<fpage>10838</fpage>&#x02013;10844.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10753878</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal">Thome, M., and J. Tschopp. <year>2001</year>. Regulation of lymphocyte proliferation and death by FLIP. <source>Nat. Rev. Immunol.</source> <volume>1</volume>:<fpage>50</fpage>&#x02013;58.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11905814</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ghosh, S., and M. Karin. <year>2002</year>. Missing pieces in the NF-kappaB puzzle. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>109</volume>:<fpage>S81</fpage>&#x02013;S96.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11983155</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal">Hayden, M.S., and S. Ghosh. <year>2004</year>. Signaling to NF-kappaB. <source>Genes Dev.</source> <volume>18</volume>:<fpage>2195</fpage>&#x02013;2224.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15371334</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal">Chaudhary, P.M., M.T. Eby, A. Jasmin, A. Kumar, L. Liu, and L. Hood. <year>2000</year>. Activation of the NF-kappaB pathway by caspase 8 and its homologs. <source>Oncogene.</source> <volume>19</volume>:<fpage>4451</fpage>&#x02013;4460.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11002417</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kataoka, T., and J. Tschopp. <year>2004</year>. N-terminal fragment of c-FLIP(L) processed by caspase 8 specifically interacts with TRAF2 and induces activation of the NF-kappaB signaling pathway. <source>Mol. Cell. Biol.</source> <volume>24</volume>:<fpage>2627</fpage>&#x02013;2636.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15024054</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal">Hur, G.M., J. Lewis, Q. Yang, Y. Lin, H. Nakano, S. Nedospasov, and Z.G. Liu. <year>2003</year>. The death domain kinase RIP has an essential role in DNA damage-induced NF-kappa B activation. <source>Genes Dev.</source> <volume>17</volume>:<fpage>873</fpage>&#x02013;882.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12654725</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Liu, Z.G. <year>2005</year>. Molecular mechanism of TNF signaling and beyond. <source>Cell Res.</source> <volume>15</volume>:<fpage>24</fpage>&#x02013;27.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15686622</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal">Peter, M.E., and P.H. Krammer. <year>2003</year>. The CD95(APO-1/Fas) DISC and beyond. <source>Cell Death Differ.</source> <volume>10</volume>:<fpage>26</fpage>&#x02013;35.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12655293</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal">Boatright, K.M., M. Renatus, F.L. Scott, S. Sperandio, H. Shin, I.M. Pedersen, J.E. Ricci, W.A. Edris, D.P. Sutherlin, D.R. Green, and G.S. Salvesen. <year>2003</year>. A unified model for apical caspase activation. <source>Mol. Cell.</source> <volume>11</volume>:<fpage>529</fpage>&#x02013;541.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12620239</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal">Boatright, K.M., C. Deis, J.B. Denault, D.P. Sutherlin, and G.S. Salvesen. <year>2004</year>. Activation of caspases-8 and -10 by FLIP(L). <source>Biochem. J.</source> <volume>382</volume>:<fpage>651</fpage>&#x02013;657.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15209560</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">Schmitz, I., H. Weyd, A. Krueger, S. Baumann, S.C. Fas, P.H. Krammer, and S. Kirchhoff. <year>2004</year>. Resistance of short term activated T cells to CD95-mediated apoptosis correlates with de novo protein synthesis of c-FLIPshort. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>172</volume>:<fpage>2194</fpage>&#x02013;2200.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14764686</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal">Fulda, S., E. Meyer, and K.M. Debatin. <year>2000</year>. Metabolic inhibitors sensitize for CD95 (APO-1/Fas)-induced apoptosis by down-regulating Fas-associated death domain-like interleukin 1-converting enzyme inhibitory protein expression. <source>Cancer Res.</source> <volume>60</volume>:<fpage>3947</fpage>&#x02013;3956.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10919673</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal">Su, H., N. Bidere, L. Zheng, A. Cubre, K. Sakai, J. Dale, L. Salmena, R. Hakem, S. Straus, and M. Lenardo. <year>2005</year>. Requirement for caspase-8 in NF-kappaB activation by antigen receptor. <source>Science.</source> <volume>307</volume>:<fpage>1465</fpage>&#x02013;1468.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15746428</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kennedy, N.J., T. Kataoka, J. Tschopp, and R.C. Budd. <year>1999</year>. Caspase activation is required for T cell proliferation. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>190</volume>:<fpage>1891</fpage>&#x02013;1896.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10601363</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal">Misra, R.S., D.M. Jelley-Gibbs, J.Q. Russell, G. Huston, S.L. Swain, and R.C. Budd. <year>2005</year>. Effector CD4&#x0002b; T cells generate intermediate caspase activity and cleavage of caspase-8 substrates. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>174</volume>:<fpage>3999</fpage>&#x02013;4009.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15778357</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal">Chau, H., V. Wong, N.J. Chen, H.L. Huang, W.J. Lin, C. Mirtsos, A.R. Elford, M. Bonnard, A. Wakeham, A.I. You-Ten, et al. <year>2005</year>. Cellular FLICE-inhibitory protein is required for T cell survival and cycling. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>202</volume>:<fpage>405</fpage>&#x02013;413.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16043518</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal">Chun, H.J., L. Zheng, M. Ahmad, J. Wang, C.K. Speirs, R.M. Siegel, J.K. Dale, J. Puck, J. Davis, C.G. Hall, et al. <year>2002</year>. Pleiotropic defects in lymphocyte activation caused by caspase-8 mutations lead to human immunodeficiency. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>419</volume>:<fpage>395</fpage>&#x02013;399.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12353035</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><label>31</label><citation citation-type="journal">Dohrman, A., T. Kataoka, S. Cuenin, J.Q. Russell, J. Tschopp, and R.C. Budd. <year>2005</year>. Cellular FLIP (long form) regulates CD8&#x0002b; T cell activation through caspase-8-dependent NF-kappa B activation. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>174</volume>:<fpage>5270</fpage>&#x02013;5278.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15843523</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><label>32</label><citation citation-type="journal">Scaffidi, C., J.P. Medema, P.H. Krammer, and M.E. Peter. <year>1997</year>. FLICE is predominantly expressed as two functionally active isoforms, caspase-8/a and caspase-8/b. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>272</volume>:<fpage>26953</fpage>&#x02013;26958.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9341131</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><label>33</label><citation citation-type="journal">Trauth, B.C., C. Klas, A.M. Peters, S. Matzku, P. Moller, W. Falk, K.M. Debatin, and P.H. Krammer. <year>1989</year>. Monoclonal antibody-mediated tumor regression by induction of apoptosis. <source>Science.</source> <volume>245</volume>:<fpage>301</fpage>&#x02013;305.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2787530</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib34"><label>34</label><citation citation-type="journal">Brenner, D., A. Golks, F. Kiefer, P.H. Krammer, and R. Arnold. <year>2005</year>. Activation or suppression of NFkappaB by HPK1 determines sensitivity to activation-induced cell death. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>24</volume>:<fpage>4279</fpage>&#x02013;4290.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16341093</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib35"><label>35</label><citation citation-type="journal">Laemmli, U.K. <year>1970</year>. Cleavage of structural proteins during the assembly of the head of bacteriophage T4. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>227</volume>:<fpage>680</fpage>&#x02013;685.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5432063</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib36"><label>36</label><citation citation-type="journal">Medema, J.P., C. Scaffidi, F.C. Kischkel, A. Shevchenko, M. Mann, P.H. Krammer, and M.E. Peter. <year>1997</year>. FLICE is activated by association with the CD95 death-inducing signaling complex (DISC). <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>16</volume>:<fpage>2794</fpage>&#x02013;2804.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9184224</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib37"><label>37</label><citation citation-type="journal">Klas, C., K.M. Debatin, R.R. Jonker, and P.H. Krammer. <year>1993</year>. Activation interferes with the APO-1 pathway in mature human T cells. <source>Int. Immunol.</source> <volume>5</volume>:<fpage>625</fpage>&#x02013;630.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7688561</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>